---
// Terms of use. PRIVACY_AND_COMPLIANCE.md §7 item 2 — "including the anti-scam
// statement and the 18+ requirement".
//
// Written to be read. A term nobody reads is a term nobody can rely on, and the
// two that matter most here — we never charge you to apply, and we are not the
// organiser — are the first two things on the page.

import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { BRAND, CONTACT, NO_FEE_STATEMENT } from "@mbele/config";
---

<Base
  title="Terms of use"
  description={`The terms you agree to by using ${BRAND.name}.`}
  canonical="/terms"
>
  <article class="max-w-prose">
    <h1 class="text-title font-bold tracking-[-0.015em]">Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-dense text-ink-2">
      Plain English, because terms you cannot read are terms you cannot rely on.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-subtitle font-semibold">We never charge you to apply</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 border-l-[3px] border-brand bg-brand-wash p-3 text-dense font-semibold">
      {NO_FEE_STATEMENT}
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-dense">
      We do not list opportunities that charge an application fee, and we never ask you for money to
      use this site, to apply for anything, or to be "considered". Nobody from here will ever
      message you asking for a payment, a fee, or your bank details. If that happens, it is not us —
      <a href="/anti-scam" class="text-brand">here is how to tell</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-subtitle font-semibold">We are not the organiser</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-dense">
      Every opportunity here belongs to somebody else. We collect and structure what organisers
      publish, show you the source, and say when we last checked it. We do not decide who wins, we
      cannot influence an application, and we cannot answer questions about someone else's process.
      The official page is always the authority — and where we disagree with it, believe it, not us.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-subtitle font-semibold">Eligibility answers are guidance</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-dense">
      When we say you are eligible, we mean the organiser's own published rules, as quoted on the
      page, match the details you gave us. We show you the exact sentence we based it on so you can
      check our reading. It is not a decision, a guarantee, or advice. When we are not sure we say
      "unclear" rather than guessing, and "unclear" never means "do not apply".
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-subtitle font-semibold">You need to be 18</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-dense">
      Accounts here are for people aged 18 and over. Some listed opportunities accept under-18s and
      we keep listing them, because removing them would help nobody — but you must be 18 to hold an
      account. Until you confirm it, you can read everything and check your eligibility, and the
      features that connect you to other people stay off. This is a deliberate trade: a
      small independent product should not be running an unmoderated contact surface for minors.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-subtitle font-semibold">What we ask of you</h2>
    <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-dense">
      <li>Be honest in what you post. Made-up projects and borrowed work waste other people's time.</li>
      <li>Do not use this to recruit for anything that charges people to take part.</li>
      <li>Do not harass anyone, and do not contact people who have not asked to hear from you.</li>
      <li>Do not scrape the site or hammer it with automated requests. Ask us instead — we may just give you the data.</li>
      <li>One account per person.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-2 text-dense text-ink-2">
      The full rules on content and behaviour are on the
      <a href="/content-policy" class="text-brand">content policy</a> page, including what happens
      when they are broken and how to appeal.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-subtitle font-semibold">Your content stays yours</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-dense">
      Anything you write — your profile, your projects, your notes — belongs to you. By posting it
      you let us show it to the people you chose to show it to, and nothing more. Your tracker and
      your notes are private, including from us in every routine sense: no administrator has a path
      to read them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-subtitle font-semibold">When we might restrict an account</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-dense">
      If someone is being harmed, we act first and explain afterwards, in that order. A restricted
      account can still read everything, check eligibility and keep its tracker; what stops is
      contacting other people. You will be told what happened and why, and you can appeal to
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.support}`} class="text-brand">{CONTACT.support}</a>. This is
      protection, not punishment, and it is reversible.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-subtitle font-semibold">No promises we cannot keep</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-dense">
      This is a small product run on free infrastructure. It will occasionally be slow, and it will
      occasionally be down. We will not promise uptime we cannot deliver. What we do promise: we
      never lose your data silently, everything you can see you can export, and if we cannot serve a
      page we say so rather than showing you something wrong.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-subtitle font-semibold">If something here is wrong</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-dense">
      Report it from the opportunity page — it takes one tap and you do not need an account. If you
      are an organiser and something about your opportunity is wrong, or you want it removed, write
      to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.takedown}`} class="text-brand">{CONTACT.takedown}</a> and we
      act within 48 hours, without argument.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-8 text-micro text-ink-2">
      Changes to these terms appear on the <a href="/changelog" class="text-brand">changelog</a>
      with the date and a one-line summary.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
